// How the zip reader gives up. Moved out of lib/zip/inf, which is gone now
// that idstd holds the DEFLATE decoder: this was never about inflation, it is
// the one abort path zip_bytes, zip_dir, zip_need, zip_sig and zip_infl all
// share.
//
// There are no exceptions and no early return, so a malformed archive cannot
// be reported upwards: it would have to be threaded through every frame as a
// flag, and every caller would have to gate on it. Saying what is wrong and
// aborting is the honest alternative -- an editor that opened a broken file
// and showed an empty document would be worse than one that stopped. The pop
// of an empty list is what does the aborting: it is `id`'s trap, so this
// exits 1 with a line on stderr as well as the line above on stdout.
zip_fail(string s) {
  int[] xs = [];
  print("id: " + s);
  pop(xs);
} return void;
("zip: bad record signature"):() then traps:("id: pop from empty list")
("zip: no end-of-central-directory record"):() then traps:("id: pop from empty list")
